{
    "background_story": "Ashlynn was a brilliant and meticulous watchmaker who spent most of her days hunched over a workbench, surrounded by gears, springs, and delicate mechanisms. Her specialty was restoring antique timepieces to their former glory, and she took great pride in her work. Ashlynn's favorite tool was her trusty vernier caliper, which she used to measure the tiniest components with precision. With it, she could detect even the slightest deviations in the intricate dance of gears and balance wheels. One day, a rare 19th-century pocket watch came into her shop, its mechanism badly damaged. Ashlynn spent weeks painstakingly repairing it, using her vernier caliper to ensure every part was perfectly aligned. When the watch was finally restored, its owner was overjoyed, and Ashlynn's reputation as a master watchmaker was solidified.",
